      "sequence_position": 11,
      "problem": "If $A=\\{2,3\\}$ and $B=∅$ then $|P(A\\times P(B))|=$",
      "worked_solution": "For any set $S,$ we have $|P(S)|={2}^{|S|}.$ Also, $|S\\times T|=|S|\\cdot |T|.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n|A|=2,\\,|B|=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n|P(B)|={2}^{|B|}={2}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|P(A\\times P(B))| & ={2}^{|A\\times P(B)|} \\\\  & ={2}^{|A|\\,\\cdot \\,P(B)} \\\\  & ={2}^{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & ={2}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
